{%- comment -%}
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THE DESIGNERS, IN ORDER (Corvo addition)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Prints the handles of the "Designer" entries in Shopify (Content > Metaobjects), separated by commas, in the order of
the lists: first the designers with a number in "Order in the lists", lowest first, then the others in alphabetical
order. A designer ticked "Preview only" is left out on the published theme.

Every list of designers reads its order here: the Designers page, the header panel, the site search and the guide
for AI assistants. Liquid cannot sort entries by one of their fields, so each entry gets a key that sorts as text.
A caller reads an entry back with shop.metaobjects.designer[handle].

The list holds up to fifty designers: an entry list read without pagination stops there, and this snippet is used
inside paginated pages, where a second pagination is not allowed.

********************************************
Supported variables
********************************************

* exclude: the handle of a designer to leave out (optional), such as the designer whose page is open
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign designer_items = ''

  for designer in shop.metaobjects.designer.values
    if designer.example.value and theme.role == 'main'
      continue
    endif

    if exclude != blank and designer.system.handle == exclude
      continue
    endif

    assign designer_number = 99999

    if designer.position.value != blank
      assign designer_number = designer.position.value | plus: 0 | at_least: 0 | at_most: 49999
    endif

    assign designer_order = designer_number | prepend: '00000' | slice: -5, 5
    assign designer_name_key = designer.name.value | default: designer.system.handle | downcase
    assign designer_items = designer_items | append: designer_order | append: ':' | append: designer_name_key | append: '§' | append: designer.system.handle | append: '¦'
  endfor

  assign designer_sorted = designer_items | split: '¦' | sort
  assign designer_handles = ''

  for designer_item in designer_sorted
    assign designer_handle = designer_item | split: '§' | last

    if designer_handles != ''
      assign designer_handles = designer_handles | append: ','
    endif

    assign designer_handles = designer_handles | append: designer_handle
  endfor

  echo designer_handles
-%}
